{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"69d144badc45031b6fcf10bd8cc445ae5f5ea909c56572cea7ee45e4339ef7d4","digest":{"component_or_area":"documentation CI validation","key_entities":["docs/README.md","docs/*.md","scripts/check_docs_index.py",".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","*.local.md"],"problem_keywords":["documentation index","dead links","link validation","ci gate","drift detection","broken relative links"],"propositions":["Every living top-level docs/*.md file must be linked from docs/README.md or be on an explicit allowlist (*.local.md and designated historical docs), otherwise the CI gate fails","Any relative markdown link within docs/ that points to a nonexistent docs/… target must be caught and cause the gate to fail","A new script check_docs_index.py must enumerate docs/*.md files, parse links from docs/README.md, and validate all relative internal markdown links","The check must be integrated into both .github/workflows/test.yml and .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml CI pipelines","The gate prevents index-completeness drift from recurring silently by making unindexed living docs and broken relative links deterministically detectable"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785825365811088385,"uuid":"2a77c106-b3ae-4e02-bbb0-63e0ebff0081"}